In SQLite (an ordinary table, not `STRICT`), what does this program print? Write the four lines separated by single spaces.

```sql
CREATE TABLE t (x INTEGER);
INSERT INTO t VALUES ('12'), ('1.5'), ('abc'), (3.0);
SELECT typeof(x) FROM t;
```

What number does this program print?

```sql
CREATE TABLE score (player TEXT PRIMARY KEY, points INTEGER NOT NULL);
INSERT INTO score VALUES ('Ana', 10), ('Bo', 7);
INSERT INTO score VALUES ('Ana', 5), ('Chen', 4)
ON CONFLICT (player) DO UPDATE SET points = points + excluded.points;
UPDATE score SET points = points * 2 WHERE points < 10;
SELECT sum(points) FROM score;
```

This script is run in the sqlite3 shell **without** `-bail`, so it continues after errors. Which stations end up in the table? List their letters.

```sql
CREATE TABLE reading (
  station TEXT NOT NULL,
  celsius REAL CHECK (celsius BETWEEN -90 AND 60)
);
INSERT INTO reading VALUES ('A', 21.5);
INSERT INTO reading VALUES ('B', NULL);
INSERT INTO reading VALUES ('C', 75);
INSERT INTO reading VALUES (NULL, 10);
INSERT INTO reading VALUES ('E', -5);
```

What does this program print?

```sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
CREATE TABLE author (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE poem (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  author_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES author (id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  title TEXT NOT NULL
);
INSERT INTO author VALUES (1, 'Hafez'), (2, 'Rumi'), (3, 'Basho');
INSERT INTO poem (author_id, title) VALUES
  (1, 'a'), (1, 'b'), (2, 'c'), (3, 'd'), (3, 'e'), (3, 'f');
DELETE FROM author WHERE id <> 2;
SELECT count(*) FROM poem;
```
